; The facade look the city actually loads, shared by every tile.
;
; `tools/generated_scene_import.gd` maps the ETL's `city_facade` material name to
; this path and only this path, so this file *is* the switch: it currently names
; `city_facade_clean.gdshader`, and `city_facade_warm.tres` beside it names the
; measured `city_facade.gdshader`. Both read the same `TEXCOORD_0` payload, so
; swapping is a copy and a reimport — never a rebuild.
;
; Here rather than as shader defaults because CLAUDE.md hard rule 4 makes tuning
; data, not constants — and beside `golden_hour.tres` because the sun these are
; judged under is tuned in the same directory. Loaded as **one** resource for all
; 66 tiles: retuning the city is this file.
;
; `floor_height_m` is still the measured 2.8 m and stays that way whichever
; shader is loaded — the massing is real and the floor rhythm should be. What the
; clean look changes is the *scale everything else is drawn at*: glazing spans a
; group of storeys and a bay is 9 m, because the measured 2.4 m column pitch is
; about four pixels across from a moving car and reads as noise rather than as
; architecture. See the shader header.
;
; ✅ **The facade elements are ON: this file ships the `A‴` look** — the seven
; fabric values below plus the surveyed verdicts at `survey_apply = 1.0` and
; `P3-7a`'s `W1`/`W2` corrections. User's call, 2026-08-09, from the `A‴`
; frames ("much more acceptable now"), confirmed from the driver's seat. From
; 2026-08-06 to then the look was parked to massing plus flat colour — the
; window grid was competing with the per-building colour rather than adding to
; it — and what changed the judgment is `W1`/`W2`: punched openings became
; glass and the panes stopped repeating.
;
; **Seven parameters hold the switch, and it takes all seven** (plus
; `survey_apply`). `solid_share = 1.0` is the gate: `glazed = step(solid_share,
; …)` in the shader, so at 1.0 no building is ever glazed and the curtain-wall,
; fin and punched types stop drawing. That alone leaves the street-level
; furniture behind — measured, 86% of the frame still differed — because
; shopfronts, cornices, floor lines and mullions are drawn outside that gate,
; so each must be zeroed too.
;
; To park the look again — candidate `C`, still the reducibility baseline every
; remaining `P3-7a` step is proved byte-identical against — zero the eight:
;
;   solid_share 1.0 · glass_ratio 0.0 · shopfront_share 0.0 · accent_share 0.0
;   cornice_darkness 0.0 · floor_line_darkness 0.0 · mullion_darkness 0.0
;   survey_apply 0.0
;
; The shipped seven are `542cac3`'s, unchanged since that commit.
;
; The dozens of uniforms those seven make inert — `bay_width_m`, `glass_colour`,
; `pane_bow`, the fresnel terms — are left at their tuned values on purpose. They
; are the state a future art idea starts from, not dead weight to be cleaned up.
;
; ⚠️ **`base_wash` is 0.0 because the palette lives in the city config**, which
; is where the shader's header says it belongs. The `materials:` table in
; `etl/config/cities/hong_kong.yaml` carries the city's level — every colour in
; it was re-authored 19 L* darker once the anchor probe measured that as what the
; white city needed — so the wash has nothing left to trial. That leaves
; `base_colour` inert, kept at its tuned value on the same rule as the window
; uniforms above.
;
; ⚠️ Those colours used to sit inline on the height bands, and `Q34` moved them:
; the field's position asserted that material is a function of height, which 0.9%
; of measured facade lightness does not support. Nothing about the level changed.
;
; `value_jitter` 0.35 is the small half of that change and is bounded on both
; sides. Below it a block reads as one mass; above roughly 0.4 the darkest draws
; stop reading as buildings differing and start reading as a few of them being
; broken. It is not the lever that fixed the white city — at the 0.6 ceiling it
; moved the frame 0.4 L*, against 10.3 for the bands.
;
; ⚠️ **`survey_apply` is 1.0: the surveyed verdicts draw.** Since schema 6
; every tile carries the measured facade verdicts in `TEXCOORD_1` —
; reader-glazed, glass tint, grammar (`Q40`/`Q41`) — and at 1.0 the shader
; draws them, with only refusals falling back to the hash. ⚠️ Never move it
; without the seven fabric values above: against the parked values the
; overrides alone draw a half-look (surveyed curtain walls glaze while punched
; stock stays blank, because `glass_ratio` is 0.0) — that was `A′`, a defect
; and not a look. The lineage: `A″` (`Q43`, `build/driver/q43/`) fixed the
; collapsed fenestration gate; `A‴` (`P3-7a`, `build/driver/q26_A3_422ee16/`)
; added `unglazed_glassy` and the `pane_*` modulation, held the `Q30` chroma
; bar on all three audit cameras, and is what the user accepted and this file
; now ships. The `≥3`-HK-driver recognition round (`P3-9a`) still grades the
; shipped look on the web build under `Q26`.
;
; ⚠️ `recess_colour` and `unglazed_reflect` are what an opening is made of where
; the survey says glazing does not *dominate* — `punched` stock (`Q43`). Inert
; while the look is parked, on the same rule as `glass_colour` above, and
; authored rather than measured: `Q40` measured the tint of glazing, and nothing
; has measured a concrete reveal.
; `unglazed_glassy` is `Q44`'s correction to how far those two reach: the user
; judged `A″`'s punched openings — matte near-black holes on 67% of read faces —
; and called them glass. It floors the opening's glassiness where glazing does
; not dominate: 0.0 is the `Q43` behaviour exactly, 1.0 makes the opening
; material always glass with the recess reduced to frame-and-reveal. 0.65 is
; the value the user accepted on the `A‴` frames; retune it against the `Q30`
; chroma bar (mean C* cost vs `C` ≤ `A`'s on all three audit cameras), which
; it currently passes with headroom.
; The three `pane_*` values below them are `Q45`: per-building modulation of
; the hashed pane pick — `L*`/`b*` jitter in CIELAB plus a pull of the pane's
; chromaticity (the full a*b*, so near-neutral buildings pull their panes
; toward grey — deliberate, graded into `A‴`) toward the building's own
; measured `COLOR_0`. Fallback only, never
; the surveyed tint (that is a measurement), and punched panes never take the
; dark-mode tint (`Q40` conditioned it on glazed; the ETL enforces it). These
; are the values the user accepted on the `A‴` frames; the bound on retuning
; is `Q35`'s: panes should vary within a frame without a salt-and-pepper
; skyline.
; `glass_astar` is the a* the tint encoding dropped (`Q40` PCA, 6.5%), one
; value for the city, retuned at `Q26` if at all.
; The five `quiet_*` values are `Q46`'s quiet tier: where the grammar
; *refused*, the hash draws from a conservative distribution instead of
; asserting confident fenestration — the 2026-08-09 drive test's invented
; windows on plant boxes, tunnel piers and the HKCEC service base were all
; refused stock. Eligibility is the refusal itself, never height (`Q34`).
; `quiet_shopfront` and `quiet_clamp` at 1.0 are the categorical halves: a
; shopfront needs a committed grammar, and refused stock never draws a
; hash-picked curtain or fin, only punched. `quiet_pier_ratio` 0.68 (a floor
; over `punched_pier_ratio`), `quiet_solid` 0.55 (solid probability 0.27 →
; ≈0.67 on refused stock) and `quiet_pane_mute` 0.5 (fallback-pane chroma
; halved, never its glassiness — `Q44` stands) are graded values, retuned
; against the `Q30` bar. Bounds: `quiet_solid` is bounded below by the five
; drive-test sightings and above by refusal covering 35% of buildings — at
; 1.0 it would blank whole occluded mid-rise streets. All five sit behind
; `survey_apply`, so the parked recipe above needs no ninth zero.
[gd_resource type="ShaderMaterial" load_steps=2 format=3]

